# Remap the Shield remote's (2019) round centre button from KEY_SELECT to
# KEY_ENTER.
#
# The button sends HID Consumer-Control usage 0x0041 ("AC Select"), which
# hid-generic maps to Linux KEY_SELECT (evdev code 353) - confirmed via
# `evtest`, raw scancode 0xc0041. That is a legitimate keycode, but gamescope's
# Steam Game Mode UI keyboard navigation only treats Enter/Return as confirm,
# so KEY_SELECT does nothing there even though the D-pad (plain arrow keys)
# navigates fine. Kodi is unaffected either way: its default keymap has no
# binding for the "select" key name, only for "enter"/"return" (both mapped to
# the Select action) - so this remap is what makes the centre button do
# anything in Kodi too, not a regression risk.
#
# Match is scoped to this exact device (bus/vendor/product/version from its
# MODALIAS) so it cannot affect any other keyboard.
evdev:input:b0005v0955p7217e0002*
 KEYBOARD_KEY_c0041=enter

# The ◁ "back" button already sends a semantically-correct KEY_BACK (raw HID
# Consumer usage 0x0224), but gamescope's Steam UI does not bind KEY_BACK to
# anything - confirmed empirically it does nothing, while Escape does act as
# back/cancel there. Remap to Escape so it matches Xbox controller B.
evdev:input:b0005v0955p7217e0002*
 KEYBOARD_KEY_c0224=esc
